      "title": "Patanjali Foods Q1 result: Profit jumps 86% to ₹336 crore on higher income",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/quarterly-results/patanjali-foods-q1-result-profit-jumps-86-to-336-crore-on-higher-income-126081500952_1.html",
      "description": "Patanjali Foods Ltd has reported an 86 per cent increase in its consolidated net profit to Rs 335.73 crore in the quarter ended June, backed by higher total income.\nIts net profit stood at Rs 180.35 crore in the year-ago period.\nTotal income rose to Rs 11,341.89 crore during the first quarter of this fiscal from Rs 8,779 crore in the corresponding period of the preceding year, according to a regulatory filing.\nEdible oil business contributed Rs 8,504 crore revenue during the April-June period of the 2026-27 fiscal, while the FMCG vertical accounted for Rs 2937.74 crore of the total revenue.\nIncorporated in 1986, Patanjali Foods Limited is one of the leading edible oil companies in the country. The company operates in the Edible Oils, FMCG, and Wind Power Generation segments. It sells products under different brands like Patanjali, Ruchi Gold, Nutrela, Dant Kanti, Mahakosh, Sunrich, etc.\nDuring the 2025-26 fiscal, the company's net profit grew to Rs 1,814.47 crore from Rs 1,300.70",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-15T09:43:33"
    },
    {
      "title": "Brigade Enterprises sales bookings dip 5% to ₹1,061 crore in Apr-Jun",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/brigade-enterprises-sales-bookings-dip-5-to-1-061-crore-in-apr-jun-126081500797_1.html",
      "description": "Realty firm Brigade Enterprises Ltd's sales bookings fell 5 per cent to Rs 1,061 crore during the first quarter of this fiscal on lower volumes.\nIts sales bookings or pre-sales stood at Rs 1,118 crore in the year-ago period.\nIn its latest investor presentation, the company said it achieved pre-sales of Rs 1,061 crore with a volume of 0.74 million sq ft in the April-June quarter of the 2026-27 fiscal.\nThe sales volumes dropped 22 per cent from 0.94 million sq ft in the first quarter of the last financial year.\nHowever, the average sales realisation stood at Rs 14,256 per sq ft during the June quarter, a growth of 21 per cent over the year-ago period.\nBengaluru-based Brigade Enterprises is one of the leading real estate developers in the country.\nRecently, the company reported a 37 per cent increase in its consolidated net profit to Rs 216.94 crore for the quarter ended June.\nIts net profit stood at Rs 157.95 crore in the year-ago period.\nTotal income fell to Rs 1,179.22 crore in",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-15T08:18:31"
    }
  ]
